invariant: INV-39
file: srv_handshake.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-blocking server completes on a client Finished that has
  bytes after it in its record, and srv_complete drops them. RFC 9846
  section 5.1 makes that unexpected_message. test/tcp_blocking_loop_test.c
  seals the Finished with one byte after it and requires that alert.

--- old
    rc = srv_read_client_finished(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
    // The read key changes after the client Finished, so the Finished must
    // end its record (hsr_check_record_end) before srv_complete runs.
    return hsr_check_record_end(h);
--- new
    return srv_read_client_finished(h);
